{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1273333-portal","id":1273333,"title":"Portal","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-07T14:58:48-08:00","id":1273333,"title":"Portal","content":"So, what's the difference between a portal made with correspondence 3 and 4, besides its size?<br /> Can Cor 3 transport a person other than the mage? What would be the size limit for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T09:14:57-08:00","id":1273733,"title":"","content":"Per page 79 in &quot;How Do You DO That?&quot; Correspondence 3 portals are self-only and short-lived. Correspondence 4 allows a longer lasting gate/portal. 10 successes allows a small permanent portal with additional successes required to make it bigger and additional successes required to set the distance per the Teleportation Range charge. I couldn't find anything specifically about size but I'd do something like &quot;an additional success for each size of the gate beyond a standard door exterior (80&quot; x 36&quot; in the US).<br /> <br /> Correspondence 3 plus other spheres allows the mage to temporarily pierce space and pull or push patterns with appropriate other spheres. Life 3 to grab a person, Matter 3 to grab a lump of matter, and some number of successes for distance and size for things beyond the size of a person. I can't find a direct source as to whether additional. Note, I've found inconsistencies in that part in that some sources say you need other spheres and others don't mention it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":15603,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","user":"PhillyCuriosity","date":". 12-10-2018, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T11:52:59-08:00","id":1273761,"title":"","content":"I see. So what's stopping someone from entering the correspondence 3 portal right after/before the mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T12:12:46-08:00","id":1273765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1273333-portal?p=1273761#post1273761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. So what's stopping someone from entering the correspondence 3 portal right after/before the mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing but practicality intercedes. Usually effects aren't instantaneous (the whole focus thing) and the person casting has to &quot;aim&quot; as well (to get the portal in the right place). Usually to throw someone into a portal you add forces to give them a push and you have some kind of resisted roll of the success of the forces portion vs the recipient's strength. This requires additional success so this isn't exactly trivial to cast until someone has relatively high arete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T05:30:01-08:00","id":1273871,"title":"","content":"If it's &quot;self-only&quot; then it stands to reason that only &quot;oneself&quot; can enter through it.<br /> <br /> If you want a metaphysical explanation: Perhaps the &quot;portal&quot; it's located in your pattern (or the target pattern) and/or it's only capable of translocating one particular pattern defined at the moment of the casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T06:03:44-08:00","id":1273874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1273333-portal?p=1273871#post1273871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want a metaphysical explanation: Perhaps the &quot;portal&quot; it's located in your pattern (or the target pattern) and/or it's only capable of translocating one particular pattern defined at the moment of the casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if you don't like to use the word &quot;pattern&quot;, because Corr isn't a Pattern Sphere, (I merely used that word because it's Mage word for &quot;object&quot;) think that it works trough the same principle that allows any Sphere to alter your senses (like, to &quot;sense space&quot;) without using Life to alter your sensory organs or Mind to alter your conscience. You're affecting a pattern trough something that isn't a pattern.<br /> Magick &quot;knows&quot; the difference between &quot;self&quot; and &quot;others&quot;, and perhaps even between individual targets without entering in the minutiae of what constitutes the pattern each target (this is all part of the targeting system - even if you don't divide successes between targets to &quot;alter self&quot; it's always easier than to affect others) - this difference allows to know what a spell can affect and what it can't affect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-11-2018, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T08:43:20-08:00","id":1273895,"title":"","content":"So, you are saying that if a mage uses correspondence 3 to open a portal to somewhere and another person tries to run into the portal before the mages does (or even after, considering it didn't close yet), rhe person would bang in the portal like if it was a closed door?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T09:11:35-08:00","id":1273899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1273333-portal?p=1273895#post1273895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you are saying that if a mage uses correspondence 3 to open a portal to somewhere and another person tries to run into the portal before the mages does (or even after, considering it didn't close yet), rhe person would bang in the portal like if it was a closed door?</div> </div> </div> </div>More like phase through it, like it was an illusion.<br /> <br /> That's assuming it has any visual appearance whatsoever and isn't just somebody disappearing on thin air - note that this effect won't necessarily allow light to travel between the two points either (albeit it <i>could</i> because scrying it's Corr 2, it all depends on how the spell it's framed and number of successes). In that case the portal would be invisible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T10:36:29-08:00","id":1273909,"title":"","content":"How it doesn't work depends on the Mage's practices and the narrative the storyteller and players have put together. There are a lot of different ways the portal can manifest from an extremely short duration hole in the air, to a portal that is literally only open wide enough for whatever part of the Mage is passing through it at that moment, to something that most people wouldn't even recognize as a portal. I imagine a CoX portal might look like a hall or passageway they never noticed before that leads where they want to go, and no one else can follow because no one else is in the right mental state to see it. They probably have a really hard time seeing what the Ecstatic even did.<br /> <br /> Don't treat it like some kind of arbitrary limit the universe is enforcing*. Instead, try to describe the portal in a way that makes it clear why it is one person only.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Unless, of course, it is part of the Mage's paradigm. If a Hermetic summons an angel to open a portal, you can absolutely have the angel block anyone else who tries to use the portal. That would be a fun scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-11T13:58:15-08:00","id":1273945,"title":"","content":"Regardless of paradigm or how the portal is created, the mage can't make a portal for him and a friend of his to go through just with Correspondence 3, then...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T04:30:08-08:00","id":1274013,"title":"","content":"Is that getting in the way of the story?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T04:30:57-08:00","id":1274014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1273333-portal?p=1273895#post1273895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you are saying that if a mage uses correspondence 3 to open a portal to somewhere and another person tries to run into the portal before the mages does (or even after, considering it didn't close yet), rhe person would bang in the portal like if it was a closed door?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it should require Correspondence 3 ( maybe lower ) and maybe Time 1 ( to get the right feel of the moment ) to travel through another Mage's Correspondence 3 pierced space immediately after she or he casts the Effect ; and only if they do it in a way that allows for this possibility, which varies based on the Mage, her or his Paradigm, the specifics of the particular Effect cast, and the circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T06:05:38-08:00","id":1274026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1273333-portal?p=1274014#post1274014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it should require Correspondence 3 ( maybe lower ) and maybe Time 1 ( to get the right feel of the moment ) to travel through another Mage's Correspondence 3 pierced space immediately after she or he casts the Effect ; and only if they do it in a way that allows for this possibility, which varies based on the Mage, her or his Paradigm, the specifics of the particular Effect cast, and the circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I'm trying to find out. If the caster wants, he can make a portal for people other than him to go through with only Corr 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-12T07:17:02-08:00","id":1274032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20 Correspondence 3, p 513</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now the mage can tear holes in space, large enough for her to step through. These minor gates are small and temporary, but they allow that character to step from one place to another, so long as she\u2019s alone and lightly encumbered (Teleporting large items ... demands Correspondence 4)<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Also, by combining Correspondence 3 with Forces, Life, or Matter, the mage can move things around from a distance, levitating, manipulating or teleporting them without physical contact.</div> </div> </div> </div>BY a strict reading of the Sphere I would say no. The holes allow &quot;that&quot; character (the mage) to step from one place to another (not &quot;any&quot; character) as long as she's alone and isn't carrying anything heavy. The intention it's clearly to make this a &quot;self-only&quot; effect. Latter it mentions teleporting stuff that isn't in direct physical contact with your body, and it says that you need other Spheres to teleport them.<br /> <br /> Debatably, you could be able to teleport someone else with Corr 3/Life 3, as long as he isn't carrying large items or heavy loads.<br /> <br /> Then again, Mage often benefits from a sligthly less literal reading: At the very least, if I were to allow this with Corr 3 alone, the gate has to be unipersonal (in the mechanics): You would need to open one door per person (again, mechanically, in the narration this can be seen any number of ways) which would need you to multiply the amount of successes by the number of people teleported (I.E: If you can teleport yourself with 3 successes, you would need 6 to teleport your friend, posibly 7 since affecting others it's always harder). \u200bYou COULD represent/narrate this as opening one door for everyone, but mechanically it will be like opening two+ doors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-12-2018, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T12:32:02-08:00","id":1274236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1273333-portal?p=1274026#post1274026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what I'm trying to find out. If the caster wants, he can make a portal for people other than him to go through with only Corr 3?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think portals in M:tA are stable long-lasting or permament warps in space that allow for travel. I presume you are asking about a Mage teleporting other persons with Correspondence 3. I would say this is possible, though the write-ups of the Sphere of Correspondence in M:tA 1st edition and M20 Corebooks don't say anything about doing so in descriptions of Correspondence 3 and 4, other than this in M20 : &quot;Also, by combining Correspondence 3 with Forces, Life, or Matter, the mage can move things around from a distance, levitating, manipulating, or teleporting them without physical contact.&quot; . It mentions combining Correspondence with Life, which definitely is an implication that Correspondence 3 can affect persons other than the Mage. And going by the description of level 3 Correspondence in 1st edition Corebook, I would also say that knowing Correspondence 3 gives a Mage such capability. I think teleporting other persons is a different Effect, and one harder to cast, than a Mage teleporting herself or himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T14:46:47-08:00","id":1274253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1273333-portal?p=1274236#post1274236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think portals in M:tA are stable long-lasting or permament warps in space that allow for travel. I presume you are asking about a Mage teleporting other persons with Correspondence 3. I would say this is possible, though the write-ups of the Sphere of Correspondence in M:tA 1st edition and M20 Corebooks don't say anything about doing so in descriptions of Correspondence 3 and 4, other than this in M20 : &quot;Also, by combining Correspondence 3 with Forces, Life, or Matter, the mage can move things around from a distance, levitating, manipulating, or teleporting them without physical contact.&quot; . It mentions combining Correspondence with Life, which definitely is an implication that Correspondence 3 can affect persons other than the Mage. And going by the description of level 3 Correspondence in 1st edition Corebook, I would also say that knowing Correspondence 3 gives a Mage such capability. I think teleporting other persons is a different Effect, and one harder to cast, than a Mage teleporting herself or himself.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I know that Correspondence 3 can teleport people, in conjunction with Life. What I really wanted to know is: If a mage cast a spell to open a portal from where he is to the Everest, would somebody also be able to enter this portal? Considering the mage wants to let people enter the portal (or don't even care). I'm asking this because just by the text of Correspondence 3 ot seems he can open portals, but only for him. And if he wanted for more people to go through as well he would need Correspondence 4. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T23:41:56-08:00","id":1274316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1273333-portal?p=1274026#post1274026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what I'm trying to find out. If the caster wants, he can make a portal for people other than him to go through with only Corr 3?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, he cannot. A mage could heal himself with Life 2, but need Life 3 to heal someone else. Likewise a mage could teleport himself with Corr 3 and couldn't do it with another person. A stable portal it's a Corr 4+ thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24623-dreamwalker","name":"Dreamwalker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T10:12:37-08:00","id":1274382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1273333-portal?p=1274253#post1274253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, I know that Correspondence 3 can teleport people, in conjunction with Life. What I really wanted to know is: If a mage cast a spell to open a portal from where he is to the Everest, would somebody also be able to enter this portal? Considering the mage wants to let people enter the portal (or don't even care). I'm asking this because just by the text of Correspondence 3 ot seems he can open portals, but only for him. And if he wanted for more people to go through as well he would need Correspondence 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that a Mage can cast a more considerable Effect that allows another person(s) to also travel to a different location. This requires Life 3, and the other persons(s) would have to immediately use the opportunity ; as per what Correspondence 3 allows for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-14-2018, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T04:17:49-08:00","id":1274539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1273333-portal?p=1274382#post1274382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that a Mage can cast a more considerable Effect that allows another person(s) to also travel to a different location. This requires Life 3, and the other persons(s) would have to immediately use the opportunity ; as per what Correspondence 3 allows for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've read the rules one more time and must say, that you're right. It is possible to teleport someone with Corr 3 and a proper Pattern Sphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24623-dreamwalker","name":"Dreamwalker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T12:09:04-08:00","id":1274598,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying just teleporting, but opening a portal with Corr 3. No other sphere involved..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T13:20:05-08:00","id":1274614,"title":"","content":"How does &quot;opening a portal&quot; differ from &quot;teleportation&quot; in regard to Correspondence 3 Effects ? I am confused by you making a differentiation between these two terms. As far as I understand it, in practical use of Correspondence 3, they are interchangeable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T04:02:51-08:00","id":1274684,"title":"","content":"Well, when you teleport someone directly you don't give the chance to other people to teleport too. A portal is like a door that allow anyone to teleport as long as it is there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T05:13:40-08:00","id":1274694,"title":"","content":"I think Correspondence 4 is needed for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T04:49:23-08:00","id":1274861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1273333-portal?p=1274684#post1274684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, when you teleport someone directly you don't give the chance to other people to teleport too. A portal is like a door that allow anyone to teleport as long as it is there.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've listed two differences there. 1) That it works for anyone, and 2) that it keeps working as long as it is active. A correspondence 3 portal could only accomplish the latter, so it would be a door (or other lasting thing) that allows the caster to teleport (or move) between two locations as long as it is there. To allow additional things through the portal the Mage would have to use additional Spheres to set more targets or upgrade to Correspondence 4 to allow everything.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T05:23:38-08:00","id":1274870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1273333-portal?p=1274861#post1274861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You've listed two differences there. 1) That it works for anyone, and 2) that it keeps working as long as it is active. A correspondence 3 portal could only accomplish the latter, so it would be a door (or other lasting thing) that allows the caster to teleport (or move) between two locations as long as it is there. To allow additional things through the portal the Mage would have to use additional Spheres to set more targets or upgrade to Correspondence 4 to allow everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree. As others already have suggested, looks like with Corr 3 the portal doesn't let anyone go through other than the mage. It is not directly stated in the books though.<br /> So, Corr 3 only you can open a portal that only you can pass (others go throu without teleporting, like if it was an illusion)<br /> Corr 3/Life 3 let other people teleport with the portal<br /> Corr4 opens a portal that anyone can teleport with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T05:44:04-08:00","id":1274874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1273333-portal?p=1274870#post1274870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agree. As others already have suggested, looks like with Corr 3 the portal doesn't let anyone go through other than the mage. It is not directly stated in the books though.<br /> So, Corr 3 only you can open a portal that only you can pass (others go throu without teleporting, like if it was an illusion)</div> </div> </div> </div>What it would look like would depend heavily on the Mage who cast it, but yes, a visible portal that most people pass through without teleporting is one way it could manifest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Corr 3/Life 3 let other people teleport with the portal </div> </div> </div>Yes. I don't know if it's anyone else or just specific people the caster sets, though. I'd probably go with specific people, though, since that makes the Corr 4 portal a significant step up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Corr4 opens a portal that anyone can teleport with. </div> </div> </div>Anyone and anything for Correspondence 4, yes. A Cor 3/Life 3 portal wouldn't let sunlight or air pass through it. A Corr 4 portal would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T11:35:44-08:00","id":1274916,"title":"","content":"Good points. To let light go through, would require Forces as well. They could be more clear about this in M20, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T09:02:28-08:00","id":1275090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1273333-portal?p=1274870#post1274870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agree. As others already have suggested, looks like with Corr 3 the portal doesn't let anyone go through other than the mage. It is not directly stated in the books though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find the descriptions of the Spheres' capabilities to be far too short throughout M:tA. They should be at least 1.5x as long as the ones in the 1st edition Corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}